# JayDB Cloud — Zero-Backend Application Architecture Rules

You are an expert AI software engineer building modern, production-grade web applications with **Zero Backend Servers**.

## Core Philosophy: Ship Apps with No Backend at All
- **No Backend Required**: Do NOT scaffold Express, FastAPI, NestJS, Go, or serverless function backends for basic data and authentication needs unless the user explicitly requests a custom server.
- **Frontend-Only**: The entire application consists of static client files (React, Vite, Next.js static export, Svelte, Vue, or Vanilla HTML/JS) hosted on GitHub Pages, Cloudflare Pages, Vercel, or S3.
- **JayDB Cloud handles both Identity and Database**: The browser communicates directly with JayDB Cloud using the official `@jaydb/cloud` SDK.

---

## 1. Authentication (OIDC + PKCE)
- **Zero Client Secrets**: Never store or require API secrets in frontend code.
- **Tenant Issuer**: The issuer is `https://<org>.jaydb.com`.
- **Public Client ID**: The app registration client ID configured in JayDB Cloud console.
- **Flow**:
  ```javascript
  import { JayDB, Auth } from '@jaydb/cloud';

  const auth = new Auth({
    issuer: 'https://acme.jaydb.com',
    clientId: 'my-web-app',
  });

  // Check login callback on app load
  if (window.location.search.includes('code=')) {
    await auth.handleCallback();
    window.history.replaceState({}, document.title, window.location.pathname);
  }

  // Sign In triggers redirect with PKCE
  function login(idp = 'google') {
    auth.signIn({ idp }); // 'google' | 'github' | 'microsoft'
  }

  function logout() {
    auth.signOut();
  }
  ```

---

## 2. Database & Data Modeling
- **Connect Database to Auth**: Pass `auth` to the `JayDB` client. It automatically attaches `Authorization: Bearer <jwt>` to all requests.
  ```javascript
  const db = new JayDB({
    baseUrl: 'https://acme.jaydb.com',
    namespace: 'production',
    auth,
  });
  ```
- **Document Key Hierarchy**: Use intuitive, REST-like URI paths:
  - `users/{userId}/profile`
  - `boards/{boardId}/metadata`
  - `boards/{boardId}/cards/{cardId}`
  - `chats/{channelId}/messages/{msgId}`

---

## 3. Concurrency & CAS (Compare-And-Swap)
JayDB uses HTTP ETags for lock-free optimistic concurrency control. Always adhere to these rules:

1. **Creating a new item**: Always use `createOnly: true` (sends `If-None-Match: *`) to guarantee you do not overwrite existing items.
   ```javascript
   await db.put('boards/proj-1/cards/c101', {
     title: 'New Card',
     status: 'todo',
     createdAt: new Date().toISOString(),
   }, { createOnly: true });
   ```

2. **Updating shared state**: Always pass `ifMatch: doc.etag` to prevent silent overwrites. Always handle `ConflictError` by re-reading:
   ```javascript
   import { ConflictError } from '@jaydb/cloud';

   async function updateCardWithRetry(cardKey, updater, maxRetries = 3) {
     for (let attempt = 0; attempt < maxRetries; attempt++) {
       const doc = await db.get(cardKey);
       if (!doc) throw new Error('Document not found');

       const updatedData = updater(doc.data);

       try {
         const newMeta = await db.put(cardKey, updatedData, {
           ifMatch: doc.etag,
         });
         return { data: updatedData, etag: newMeta.etag };
       } catch (err) {
         if (err instanceof ConflictError) {
           console.warn('Concurrent write detected, retrying...');
           continue; // re-read and retry
         }
         throw err;
       }
     }
     throw new Error('Failed to update due to high contention');
   }
   ```

3. **Deleting an item**:
   ```javascript
   await db.delete('boards/proj-1/cards/c101', { ifMatch: currentEtag });
   ```

---

## 4. Querying & Pagination
- JayDB is a document database with key and prefix access.
- List items with `db.list({ prefix, limit })` or `db.listAll({ prefix })`.
- Remember: `list` returns metadata (`key`, `etag`, `size`, `mod_time`). Only fetch full documents if the ETag changed!
  ```javascript
  const { items } = await db.list({ prefix: 'boards/proj-1/cards/', limit: 50 });
  ```

---

## 5. Collaboration & Sharing (Tree ACL)
- For invite links and shareable access tokens without server infrastructure, use `TreeACL`:
  ```javascript
  import { TreeACL } from '@jaydb/cloud';

  // Generate invite token:
  const inviteToken = await TreeACL.signInvite({
    boardId: 'proj-1',
    role: 'write',
    inviterName: auth.getUser()?.name || 'Anonymous',
    expiresInMs: 7 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000,
  });

  // Verify on receipt:
  const invite = await TreeACL.verifyInvite(inviteToken);
  ```

---

## 6. TypeScript Types
Always provide types when interacting with `@jaydb/cloud`:
```typescript
interface Card {
  title: string;
  status: 'todo' | 'in-progress' | 'done';
  assignee?: string;
}

const cardDoc = await db.get<Card>('boards/123/cards/456');
if (cardDoc) {
  console.log(cardDoc.data.title); // Type-checked
}
```
